    "summary": "High‑octane St. Paul ’82 show with scorching Bird Song & seamless Scarlet>Fire",
    "review": "August 6, 1982 at the St. Paul Civic Center was a straight‑up fire‑cracker from start to finish. The band rides a high‑energy wave that never lets up – Jerry’s guitar is on fire, Brent’s keyboards are tight as ever, and the rhythm section drives each transition with relentless momentum. Highlights include a blistering Bird Song, the classic Scarlet Begonias → Fire on the Mountain segue, a soaring Lazy Lightning → Supplication pair, and a space‑filled jam that lets the whole crew stretch out. The second set rolls through Lost Sailor → Saint of Circumstance and builds to an ecstatic Wharf Rat, all while the crowd’s excitement is captured in every note. Whether you’re a Brent‑era purist or just chasing those early‑’80s peaks, this show delivers the kind of locked‑in magic that makes St. Paul a must‑listen night.",
